{
  "_doc": "Reviewed guard mutation canaries (GHI #1154 item 5). Each record binds one reviewed mutant to one registered enforcement claim: the mutant is applied to an isolated copy of the tree and the designated test must fail. binding_sha256 is sha256 of the guard function's code (its source with docstrings and comments removed, guard_code), the claim id and the failing test id joined by newlines (src/gzkit/guard_canary.py binding_hash; code only since GHI #1311, operator 2026-11-06: \"yes, bind on code only\"); when any of them changes the canary is stale and must be re-reviewed, never silently re-hashed. A canary is enforced either way. It counts as reviewed only when .gzkit/ledger.jsonl holds a guard_canary_reviewed event at its current binding_sha256, written by `gz canary review` with the operator's verbatim words (GHI #1161); reviewed_by is a readable projection of that event, and editing it by hand marks nothing reviewed. Seeded 2026-10-02 for the refuse claims enrolled under GHI #1155.",
